   <item>
    <widget class="QLabel" name="label_2">
     <property name="text">
      <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Biscuit can fetch prices (CoinGecko), fiat exchange rates (European Central Bank), Monero crowdfunding proposals (getmonero.org) and Biscuit news (biscuitwallet.com, which keeps no logs) directly from these sources.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every Biscuit sends exactly the same requests: nothing about your wallet, balance, transactions or settings is sent. These services can see your IP address unless Tor is enabled.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you disable this, fiat conversion, Tickers, Calc and the Home tab are unavailable. You can change this at any time in the settings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
